-- A herald belongs to the definition a call resolved to. Nothing here uses a
-- definition of the same name from nlg-owner-lib.l4 or the prelude except where
-- a row says so: each rule below builds or calls something of its own.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nlg-owner-lib`

-- Records named like a heralded function: `Pt` in nlg-owner-lib.l4, `range` in
-- the prelude. A WITH body that builds one is a record literal, not a call.
DECLARE Pt HAS x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER

DECLARE range HAS low IS A NUMBER, high IS A NUMBER

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Pt
`own origin shift` n MEANS Pt WITH x IS n, y IS 100

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A range
`own band around` n MEANS range WITH low IS n, high IS 100
